    {
      "v": 22,
      "zh": "希西家慰劳一切善于事奉耶和华的利未人。于是众人吃节筵七日，又献平安祭，且向耶和华―他们列祖的　神认罪。",
      "en": "Hezekiah expressed his appreciation to all the Levites,[NOTE:1] who demonstrated great skill in serving the Lord.[NOTE:2] They feasted for the seven days of the festival[NOTE:3] and were making peace offerings and giving thanks to the Lord God of their ancestors.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “and Hezekiah spoke to the heart of all the Levites.” On the meaning of the idiom “speak to the heart of” here, see HALOT 210 s.v. II דבר 8.d.",
        "Heb “who demonstrated skill [with] good skill for the Lord.”",
        "Heb “and they ate [during] the appointed time [for] seven days.” מוֹעֵד (moʿed, “appointed time”) is probably an adverbial accusative of time referring to the festival. However, some understand it as metonymically referring to the food eaten during the festival. See BDB 417 s.v."
